abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and mathlib formalization of a basic nondegenerate analytic
  Hamiltonian KAM theorem, developed with reference to Arnold (1963)
  under explicit domain regularity assumptions. The development constructs
  the iteration, analytic invariant tori, trajectories of the original
  Hamiltonian for all real time, and a large-measure conclusion, without
  assuming a globally injective frequency map. The author has completed
  semantic self-review against the explicit mathematical statement,
  including the audit examples. Independent review and peer-review
  certification are not claimed. Equivalence with the full scope of the
  original paper is not asserted. The development used AI assistance.
